      "prompt": "Walk me through a time you had to refactor a critical backend service that was suffering from significant technical debt. How did you ensure system stability during the migration, and what specific patterns did you use to maintain performance while changing core logic?",
      "answer_outline": "A strong answer demonstrates a methodical approach: identifying bottlenecks, writing comprehensive integration tests before refactoring, and using strategies like the Strangler Fig pattern or feature flags to safely deploy changes. It should highlight the trade-offs made between code cleanliness and operational uptime.",
